ttd.tagon Title
ttd.text {Welcome to the tkEditor demo program.}
ttd.tagoff Title
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {    
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.tagon Copyright
ttd.text {Copyright © 2025, 2026 by Greg Walters and Designated Geek Software.}
ttd.tagoff Copyright
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.tagon LicenseText
ttd.text {Licensed under MIT license.}
ttd.tagoff LicenseText
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {    The tkEditor is a Tkinter Metawidget was created by ChatGPT 5.0 from a concept by Greg Walters.  This code was then turned into a Tkinter library which can be easily imported into most any Python/Tkinter program, but was originally created to be used in a PAGE GUI Designer program.
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {    SOME of the features of the tkEditor Metawidget are:
}
ttd.text {        * Auto-indent which is configurable by the user (for new text files)
}
ttd.text {        * Line numbers that scroll with the text.
}
ttd.text {        * Basic Python syntax highlighting (user configurable)
}
ttd.text {        * VERY BASIC code folding.
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {        
}
ttd.text {    The goal of this project was to create a BASIC text editor that has synced line numbers that requires ABSOLUTELY NO external libraries.  So far the tkEditor1 Metawidget keeps this requirement.  The demo program, currently DOES require at least one external library (for writing the TOML configuration file). Another goal of this project was to provide a usable Metawidget that other PAGE (and Tkinter) programmers can use for education on creation and use of Metawidgets.
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.tagon SubTitle
ttd.text {    Known Limitations...}
ttd.tagoff SubTitle
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {      At this time (5 October 2025), the biggest limitation is in the code folding routines and that the code highlighting only works for Python .py files.  Hopefully I can eventually expand this to the possibility of support of .md and .rst (Markdown and Restructured Text) files as well.  But this is in the far future at this point.
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {      One other limitation is that there is not support to convert Tabs to spaces and that changing the indent amount only works on new files.  Loading an existing file into the editor will NOT apply ANY different indentations.  This is to preserve the format of the existing file.
}
ttd.text {      
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.tagon SubTitle
ttd.text {    Still to do }
ttd.tagoff SubTitle
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {    A few things are currently on my mental list of things to do.  However, I will try to enumerate them here.
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {        * Configuration file for the program. (Uses TOML)
}
ttd.text {        * Link the preferences to the library.
}
ttd.text {        * EVENTUALLY support formatting tags (bold, italic, etc.) for the tk.ScrolledText widget in the About file.  (This file.)
}
ttd.text {        * Clean up the code in both the tkEditor and demo files.
}
ttd.text {        * Add ability to have more editors in tabs of the TNotebook.
}
ttd.text {        * Add AT LEAST popup menus for tkEditor supporting Copy, Cut, Paste
}
ttd.text {        *
}
ttd.text {        *
}
ttd.text {        *
}
ttd.text {
}
ttd.text {    For more information, please see the help document (currently unavaiable since it's creation is in process).
}
